-- title:
--   The batched preprocessing of Theorem 30, in every program beginning with base58B
-- statement:
--   For every $R$ and standard limits, `base58B ++ R` meets `PreCoreBSpec lim (base58B ++ R) cShared30`: the preprocessing preCore$(L,m,t,N,D,aX,aY,b_0)$, for a source $X$ ($K_0N\times D$, entries bounded by $U$) at `aX` and the transpose of a source $Y$ ($D\times K_0N$) at `aY`, under the limits `Lim30`, returns within `tPreCoreP cShared30 p t` steps and builds the data structure `DSReadyA` of the batched input arrays `bArrayL (stdLayout hmL) X β`, `bArrayR (stdLayout hmL) Y β` (shared stage, all tiles, tries), keeping the memory below $b_0$.
--
--   The batched layout (`Batch/Tiling`): the source of the left side is a $K_0N\times D$ matrix $X$ (row by row), that of the right side a $D\times K_0N$ matrix $Y$ (stored transposed); the slot $(g,h)$ of the band $\beta$ holds the row block number $(\beta K_0+g)K_0+h$ of the source, so one run of Theorem 30's data structure computes $K_0^2$ independent block products.
